# build / sanitizer output dirs
build*/
asan*/
tsan*/
# -DRIPWIRE_PROFILE=ON trees, same class as the three above — bench/PROFILE.md spells the dir both
# "prof" and "build_prof", so cover the prof* stem, not just profile*. Comment on its OWN line:
# gitignore has no trailing-comment syntax, so "prof*/ # why" is one literal pattern that matches nothing.
prof*/
/fuzz/
/fuzz_llvm/
/relbuild/

# incremental index caches (--cache=PATH)
*.cache
*.cache.tmp
.ripwire-cache

# generated sidecars — EPHEMERAL ONLY. --quality-baseline is re-snapshotted before every change,
# so committing it would just be noise. The DURABLE ledgers are deliberately NOT ignored:
#   .ripwire_quality_acks   accepted-debt ratchet — a per-finding decision WITH a reason. Ignored,
#                           it is a per-working-tree mute button, not a contract: it cannot reach CI,
#                           a fresh clone re-gates on debt the team already accepted, and reviewers
#                           never see the decision. It is written SORTED by (kind,key) precisely to
#                           stay merge-friendly.
#   .ripwire_arch_baseline  accepted layering debt — same argument.
#   .ripwire_notes          docs/COMMANDS.md documents this as "the committed, sorted .ripwire_notes".
.ripwire_quality_baseline
*.pptx.inspect.ndjson

# present/: the deck generator's npm tree (rebuild with `npm install` in present/)
/present/node_modules/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# bench/multiswe: downloaded raw Multi-SWE-bench per-repo JSONL (CC0, cachable, but not committed —
# see bench/multiswe/README.md; dataset.lock is the committed, derived, reproducible artifact)
/bench/multiswe/.raw-cache/

# bench/external: downloaded third-party benchmark data (Agent Retrieval Bench, SWE-Explore) —
# corpus files keep their upstream licences (SWE-Explore's dataset is CC-BY-NC-ND), so pinned +
# fetched locally, never committed or redistributed
/bench/external/
